verdict_note:
No sign-off, because of one new major finding in I28's own contract (N1); the fix is small. The fold is otherwise thorough. Of the 22 checked items, 21 are fixed and 1 (M2) is only partly fixed.
- N1 (major): the new own-commit rule picks the wrong commits outside the lead and the build branch. build_merge() takes the first first-parent merge of HEAD whose second-parent side adds docs/iterations/I28.md. On any branch that merges the lead after I28's build has landed, that merge is the branch's own 'Merge the lead' commit. R1, R2 and the per-own-commit construction checks then judge the lead's direct commits, and TestReMake reads the wrong end. Separately, if the prereg is pushed directly onto the lead, as I32's was, every later branch's commits count as I28's. Both cases were reproduced with the fold's own functions on a toy repository.
- N2 (major): this one is in I66's PR #46, on which B1's fix now relies. I66's re-scope of I32-R2 finds an empty commit list on branches based before e215fbf5 once they merge the lead, so the test fails there. Reproduced on real objects in a scratch clone, with this lane's I65 build branch as the case. It must be fixed in I66's PR before I28's build depends on it.
- Two minor residues: N3, the INHABIT.bend shape check leaves s_0, reach and the steps' arguments loose; N4, the reverting probes compare status but not reason. One note: N5, ordering and base drift.
The mechanics are clean:
- both prereg audits exit 0 ('I28: OK prereg 11c1c9322a82 ... 25 tracked functions'), and FROZEN OK;
- the 10 green-at-prereg tests pass: the 4 instrument tests, R1, R2, the 3 amended I24/I25 tests and I32's unamended R2;
- the 18 build-dependent test methods are red for the right reason, TestReMake included;
- the instrument imports no holon module and prints byte-identical output twice.
All 8 amendment lines narrow by exactly sub-form init_chain (AGENTS rule 2 holds), and the renumbered P1-P6 are each falsifiable.

